# Cloudflare Pages _redirects
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
# Generated: 2026-06-17 (task 0.6 — redirect-target map)
# Revised:   2026-06-30 (fix/redirects-cf-limit — P0-1 /shop loop + P0-2 CF rule-limit)
# Source: /projects/Bushpop/audit/url-inventory.csv (1,927 URLs)
#
# Rule ordering: CF Pages uses first-match. More-specific rules are placed BEFORE wildcards.
# Supported status codes: 200 301 302 303 307 308 (CF Pages does NOT support 410 natively).
#   200 = rewrite/serve in place (no redirect); used as the /shop/ serve-guard below.
#
# ── CF PAGES RULE-COUNT LIMIT (P0-2 fix) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CF Pages silently drops _redirects rules past an effective ceiling (the prior 186-rule file
# lost rules #131–186 → 56 women's category URLs 404'd live instead of 301→/shop). This file is
# now collapsed to well under 100 rules: the 26 explicit /uncategorized/* spam rules were dropped
# (covered by the Pages Function alone — see the 410 handling note below), and the flat
# women's/men's category slugs are collapsed into /womens-* and /mens-* splats. Keep this file
# under ~80 rules.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ── 410 SPAM HANDLING NOTE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CF Pages _redirects cannot return 410 directly, so /uncategorized/* is handled by a Pages
# Function at functions/uncategorized/[[path]].js, which returns a true 410 response.
# CF Pages precedence is _redirects > _headers > Functions > static assets, so _redirects
# must NOT contain a rule matching /uncategorized/* — that would shadow the Function and the
# spam band would 301 instead of 410 (this happened until Batch 33 Workstream B2 removed it).
# /topics/uncategorized/ (the empty spam-category archive, not part of the /uncategorized/*
# band) still legitimately 301s to /gone/ below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Rule count breakdown (actual rules in this file):
#   Section 1 slug-history:    4
#   Section 2 spam fallback:   2  (/topics/uncategorized/ + non-slash variant → /gone/)
#   Section 3 exact targets:  41  (brand 13 + auth 2 + topics 4 + app 19 + giveaways 3)
#   Section 4 splats:          6  (/shop/ guard + /shop/* + /brands/* + /source/* + 2 category)
#   Section 5 category exact:  16 (flat slugs with no shared prefix)
#   Total rules:              ~69  (well under the CF Pages effective limit)


